The same analysis was performed for the tensile deformation path of sample 9, where again the C4 T  detwinning shear was responsible for early tensile instability that occurred at ε T  = 0.41 (Table  2 , see also tensile curve of sample 9 in Fig.  6 a). Complete detwinning of deformation twin lamella led also to early tensile instability of samples 2, 3, 4, and 5 observed at strains of ε T  = 0.12, 0.47, 0.41, and 0.51, respectively (Table  2 ). As expected from minimum 1/σ Y  criterion (Fig.  2 b), this time the C3 T  detwinning shear participated in the primary stage of the tensile deformation. Since similar cases of activity of the C3 T  detwinning shear were thoroughly studied in [ 19 ,  20 ], here only the C3 T  tensile deformation path of sample 4 (see also tensile curve of sample 4 in Fig.  6 a) was checked additionally after X-ray measurements of {111} pole figures. The experimental data confirmed that rotation of the tensile axis of sample 4 occurred toward the (1  21 ¯ \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
